Description: xfail tst-ttyname — its chroot phase can't mount procfs in a container
 misc/tst-ttyname's ttyname()/ttyname_r() checks all PASS; the test then
 fails building its second chroot scenario at
 sysdeps/unix/sysv/linux/tst-ttyname.c:414, where it mounts a fresh procfs:
 .
   mount("proc", "/proc", "proc", MS_NOSUID|MS_NOEXEC|MS_NODEV, NULL)
     -> EPERM (Operation not permitted)
 .
 This is a kernel restriction, not an LSM denial: Athena's build container
 already runs with seccomp=unconfined AND apparmor=unconfined (verified —
 the glibc support/test-container tests, which also unshare+mount, now
 pass).  Mounting a new procfs instance requires the caller to OWN the PID
 namespace it mounts for; the test does unshare(CLONE_NEWNS) but not
 CLONE_NEWPID, so inside the container's shared PID namespace the kernel
 refuses.  Only --privileged with a private PID namespace, or building
 outside a container, would satisfy it — neither is a real libc concern.
 .
 Add it to the "All architectures" xfail list, next to
 tst-support_descriptors which Debian already xfails for the same
 unshare/chroot-in-container reason (bug #1070003).  With the entry the
 testsuite still runs and still fails the build on any OTHER regression;
 only this structurally-impossible test is excused.
Author: Harkirat S Virk <harkiratsvirk@gmail.com>
Origin: local
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-07-09
---
This patch header follows DEP-3: http://dep.debian.net/deps/dep3/
--- a/debian/testsuite-xfail-debian.mk
+++ b/debian/testsuite-xfail-debian.mk
@@ -15,6 +15,12 @@
 # chroot mode, see bug #1070003.
 test-xfail-tst-support_descriptors = yes

+# tst-ttyname's chroot-2 phase mounts a fresh procfs; mounting proc
+# requires PID-namespace ownership, which a container build process
+# lacks (the ttyname() checks themselves all pass).  Fails inside the
+# Athena docker build container even with seccomp+apparmor unconfined.
+test-xfail-tst-ttyname = yes
+
 ######################################################################
 # alpha (including optimized flavours)
